Z||000010||theogre||11-05-2000||11:38 PM||||I found the problem. I thought you ment you couldn't get to the site..... Should be fixed now.<P>It was caused by word. Word puts \ in layered relative links instead of /. I can't see it because it looks like IE5 automatically corrected for it. I'll have to watch for that. (I don't like the new POS server earthlink just dumped everything on. I don't like word a whole lot but it's what I got.)<P>I don't know how well it will work for IE below version 5.x. I'm not sure that article works with netscape at all. It has allot of Word2000 formating done in it. (It's heavily style sheeted and has unusual graphic treatments.)<P>Once the navigation problem is fixed, which I think it is now.... If you have problems loading it I need to know what browser you used and exactly what problem you got loading it.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-05-2000).]||||reg||1
